/-!
# Degree-19 Bernstein weights on the three-coordinate simplex

Appendix J uses all 210 triples of nonnegative exponents summing to 19.
The index order is a-major, b-minor: (a,b,19-a-b), a=0,...,19 and b=0,...,19-a.
This is the order used by the rational joint certificate data.

Generated by `scripts/generate_simplex19.py`. Generation is untrusted. The
integer tables are checked by kernel reduction, and the sixty homogeneous
marginal identities are checked as polynomial identities by `ring`.

Library search: Mathlib provides `Finset.sum_pow_eq_sum_piAntidiag` and
`Nat.multinomial_univ_three`. The explicit fixed-degree enumeration below avoids
an additional equivalence between piAntidiag and the certificate's Fin 210 order.
Mathlib's actual one-variable Bernstein polynomials, nonnegativity, and partition
of unity are reused. The module makes no claim about the Appendix J coefficients.
-/

